+++ b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-msm-gpu
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+What:           /sys/devices/.../<gpu>/gpu_busy_time_ns
+Date:           October 2026
+Contact:        linux-arm-msm@vger.kernel.org
+Description:
+                Read-only cumulative whole-GPU busy time in nanoseconds,
+                measured using the driver's gpu_busy counter. Includes work
+                from all clients. Accounting starts on the first read. The value
+                remains constant while the GPU
+                is suspended; reads do not wake the device or alter devfreq
+                governor accounting. Runtime resume preserves the cumulative
+                value and rebases the hardware counter. Driver reprobe or
+                reload resets it.
+
+                Divide the change in this value by the corresponding elapsed
+                CLOCK_MONOTONIC time to calculate a busy-time proportion.
+                This is not shader occupancy or a fraction of peak throughput.
